{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00044",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 4.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Hi, nice to see you. Sit down, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.23,
      "end_seconds": 6.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Hi. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.93,
      "end_seconds": 8.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Did you come far?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.53,
      "end_seconds": 13.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Not too far, about half an hour by bus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.35,
      "end_seconds": 15.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Right, what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.95,
      "end_seconds": 24.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a very sore throat. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.45,
      "end_seconds": 36.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "Alright, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.3,
      "end_seconds": 60.96,
      "duration_seconds": 23.66,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. It's worse with swallowing. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it. I've, I've had pain on swallowing too, uh, for about four days. About pain on swallowing, a five out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.34,
      "end_seconds": 64.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "Okay, is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.37,
      "end_seconds": 67.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.06,
      "end_seconds": 70.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Any rash or drooling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.32,
      "end_seconds": 74.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Well, I haven't had rash or drooling, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.02,
      "end_seconds": 78.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any difficulty breathing or runny nose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.16,
      "end_seconds": 82.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "So, nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.8,
      "end_seconds": 85.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.92,
      "end_seconds": 88.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.5,
      "end_seconds": 92.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.02,
      "end_seconds": 105.59,
      "duration_seconds": 11.57,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.26,
      "end_seconds": 108.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.14,
      "end_seconds": 115.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed. Clopidogrel. I take it 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.64,
      "end_seconds": 119.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.69,
      "end_seconds": 122.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.37,
      "end_seconds": 125.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.72,
      "end_seconds": 129.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "I had a bypass operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.96,
      "end_seconds": 135.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.31,
      "end_seconds": 145.07,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.61,
      "end_seconds": 151.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.36,
      "end_seconds": 155.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Oh, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.62,
      "end_seconds": 160.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.84,
      "end_seconds": 165.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Hmm, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.38,
      "end_seconds": 169.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.15,
      "end_seconds": 181.47,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "I've had asthma for about a year now. Yes, heart disease. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.03,
      "end_seconds": 197.85,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.19,
      "end_seconds": 199.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 201.33,
      "end_seconds": 207.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pressure 122 over 72, pulse is 92 beats a minute, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.34,
      "end_seconds": 223.31,
      "duration_seconds": 14.97,
      "text": "Okay, noted. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.64,
      "end_seconds": 225.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.67,
      "end_seconds": 229.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Okay, let's do a quick examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.88,
      "end_seconds": 233.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.11,
      "end_seconds": 247.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Both tonsils are red and swollen, and there are white patches on the left one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.24,
      "end_seconds": 249.11,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.15,
      "end_seconds": 251.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Open wide for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.61,
      "end_seconds": 272.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "The glands under the jaw are tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.94,
      "end_seconds": 279.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.43,
      "end_seconds": 284.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.88,
      "end_seconds": 285.69,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.93,
      "end_seconds": 321.38,
      "duration_seconds": 23.45,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Putting it all together, it fits best with tonsillitis, probably bacterial. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. It could also be a viral throat infection, so we'll keep that open. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a very sore throat, severe, and no difficulty breathing or rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.06,
      "end_seconds": 323.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.68,
      "end_seconds": 339.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.6,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.96,
      "end_seconds": 346.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.52,
      "end_seconds": 363.31,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "Let's get a throat swab, for sore throat. I'm prescribing azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for three days. That should help with throat infection. I'm prescribing paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for fever and body aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.4,
      "end_seconds": 368.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.41,
      "end_seconds": 396.4,
      "duration_seconds": 26.99,
      "text": "Finish the whole course of antibiotics even if you feel better after two days. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you can't swallow your saliva or you have trouble breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.88,
      "end_seconds": 398.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.85,
      "end_seconds": 402.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 406.57,
      "end_seconds": 408.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.32,
      "end_seconds": 416.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.66,
      "end_seconds": 426.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "So, I take the azithromycin, 500 milligrams, once a day and take the paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 427.78,
      "end_seconds": 432.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 432.89,
      "end_seconds": 435.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "I, I appreciate your time, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.54,
      "end_seconds": 437.4,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}